      "The AI tools for WhatsApp you can actually use in 2026 fall into two groups: AI built into WhatsApp, like Meta AI and the WhatsApp Business AI agent, and AI outside WhatsApp that helps you work with your chats. The right pick depends on the job: quick answers, serving customers, or making sure promises made in chat don't get forgotten.\n\n## Why can't you use ChatGPT inside WhatsApp anymore?\n\nSince 15 January 2026, Meta has banned general-purpose third-party AI chatbots, such as ChatGPT and Copilot, from running directly inside WhatsApp. In most countries, including Indonesia, the general AI assistant available inside WhatsApp is now Meta AI. Businesses can still use third-party AI, as long as it works on the business's instructions to serve its own customers.\n\nSo if you used to chat with ChatGPT on WhatsApp, you need another route. Here are five options that still work.\n\n## 1. Meta AI: the assistant built into WhatsApp\n\nMeta AI is already inside WhatsApp, so there is nothing to install. You can ask questions, create or edit images, use voice, and turn on summaries of unread messages.\n\n**Best for:** quick answers and help drafting messages.\n**Limits:** Meta AI does not message your contacts for you, and it does not keep track of promises or deadlines to remind you later.\n\n## 2. The AI agent in WhatsApp Business: for customer questions\n\nIn April 2026, WhatsApp Business announced Business AI for small and medium businesses in Indonesia, free for eligible businesses. It answers customer questions in real time using your business information, recommends products from your catalog, and lets you decide when a human takes over the conversation.\n\n**Best for:** small businesses answering the same customer questions all day.\n**Limits:** it is rolling out gradually, so check the Features tab in the WhatsApp Business app to see whether your account has it.\n\n## 3. Gemini on Android: send messages by voice\n\nOn Android phones, Gemini can help you draft and send WhatsApp messages by command, for example \"message Budi on WhatsApp and say I'm 10 minutes late\". Handy when you are driving or your hands are full.\n\n**Best for:** Android users who want to send messages without typing.\n**Limits:** Gemini does not read or summarize your WhatsApp chat history.\n\n## 4. WhatsApp API platforms with AI agents: for sales and support teams\n\nBusinesses that get a lot of chats can use a shared inbox built on the WhatsApp Business API, such as WATI or Respond.io. Several admins work from one WhatsApp number, and AI agents help answer and route chats to the right person.\n\n**Best for:** online shops and support or sales teams with several admins.\n**Limits:** paid, needs WhatsApp Business API setup, and WhatsApp charges per message. Check current pricing on their official sites.\n\n## 5. NANTI: so promises made in chat don't get forgotten\n\nThe four tools above help you reply. A different problem starts after the chat ends: \"I'll send the revision tomorrow\", \"I'll follow up with the supplier\", \"invoice goes out on the 28th\". Promises like these sink under dozens of group chats.\n\nNANTI is a web app built for that part. You paste a WhatsApp chat or upload a screenshot, NANTI records who, what and when, and reminds you in the app before the deadline. It understands Indonesian, English, mixed language and typos, and there is a free plan to try it.\n\n**Best for:** business owners, sales people and office workers who make a lot of promises in chat.\n**Limits:** for now you paste or screenshot the chat, because sending straight from WhatsApp is still being prepared.\n\n## How do you choose the right AI tool for WhatsApp?\n\nStart from the problem you hit most often, not the fanciest feature.\n\n1. Need quick answers or writing help? Use Meta AI.\n2. Customers keep asking the same things? Try the WhatsApp Business AI agent.\n3. Often sending messages while busy on Android? Use Gemini.\n4. Several admins handling customer chats? Look at a WhatsApp API platform.\n5. Forgetting promises and deadlines? Use a promise tracker like NANTI.\n\nMany businesses combine two: a WhatsApp Business AI agent to answer customers, and a promise tracker to make sure everything promised actually gets done.\n\n## Key takeaways\n\n- ChatGPT and Copilot no longer run inside WhatsApp since 15 January 2026.\n- Meta AI and the WhatsApp Business AI agent are the built-in options.\n- Gemini on Android helps send messages by command.\n- WhatsApp API platforms suit teams with several admins.\n- To track promises and deadlines from chats, use a separate tool like NANTI.\n\n## FAQ\n\n### Can I still use ChatGPT on WhatsApp?\nIn most countries, including Indonesia, no. Since 15 January 2026, Meta has banned general-purpose third-party chatbots like ChatGPT and Copilot inside WhatsApp. You can still use ChatGPT in its own app or website.\n\n### Which AI tools for WhatsApp are free?\nMeta AI is free and already inside WhatsApp. The Business AI agent in WhatsApp Business was announced as free for eligible businesses in Indonesia. NANTI has a free plan.\n\n### Can an AI app read all my WhatsApp chats?\nIt depends on the app, so check each one's privacy policy before using it. NANTI only processes the chats you paste or upload yourself and never reads your WhatsApp automatically.\n\n### What is the best AI tool for WhatsApp for a small business?\nFor customer questions, start with the AI agent in WhatsApp Business. To make sure promises to clients and suppliers are not forgotten, add a promise tracker like NANTI.",
